From 3b3aa7fc4467907964757ca869dbdd906cac6bdc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 10:51:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): upgrade VLLM_DS41_LSA to FP8 group32 dominance
 summaries and long-context r=1 shortlist

Replace the 32-byte BF16 arithmetic-mean block-8 summary in opt-in VLLM_DS41_LSA=1 (STATE_BYTES=100) with a 16-byte float8_e4m3fn Group-32 dominance-blended summary (0.85 * mean + 0.15 * k*, where k* is the key in the 8-token block with maximum squared L2 deviation from the block mean in each 32-dim MXFP4 scale group; STATE_BYTES=84), and enable the shortlist plan at r=1 decode when score_width >= 262144.

Upstream-base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Rationale: Cutting per-slot summary storage from +32 B to +16 B (STATE_BYTES 100 -> 84) halves VLLM_DS41_LSA KV cache overhead (333.57 -> 312.26 B/token, freeing +21.31 B/token across 4 indexer layers) and keeps the 1M Layer-20 summary pool (16 MB vs 32 MB) resident in GB10 L2 cache, accelerating 1M Layer-20 coarse scoring by 2.70x-2.90x and 4-layer 1M indexing to 6.10x over native while improving top-512 recall across all context lengths and needle-in-a-block regimes. Routing r=1 decode through the shortlist plan at score_width >= 262144 accelerates long-context single-row decode by up to 2.58x over native.
Quality: Default-off path (VLLM_DS41_LSA=0/unset) is 100% unchanged native indexing (68-byte keys). Under opt-in VLLM_DS41_LSA=1, FP8 Group-32 dominance summaries improve Dense b64 mean top-512 recall (87.74% vs 87.25%), Source b512 recall (95.35% vs 93.44%), Source b1024 recall (98.85% vs 97.92%; 90.7% vs 78.8% at 1M), and single-needle-in-8-token-block recall (+13.87 pp uncorrelated, +28.98 pp canceling).
Tests: pytest -v -p tblib_stub -p no:cacheprovider -p tests.kernels.deepseek_v41_pdl_sources tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_lsa.py tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_attention.py across 2 container boots (73 passed, 0 PDL violations) and 2-boot 32K-1M GPU recall and latency benchmark matrix on GB10 (sp5).
Upstream-status: local
